# Rust
/target
**/target
Cargo.lock.orig

# C++ / foobar plugin build artifacts
plugin-foobar/build/
plugin-foobar/*.dll
plugin-foobar/*.obj
plugin-foobar/*.lib
plugin-foobar/*.exp

# foobar2000 SDK: third-party, separately licensed - obtained per Plan 0001
# Phase 7, never committed.
plugin-foobar/sdk/
plugin-foobar/*.7z

# Local test audio for the headless-capture `--audio` path (Plan 0013). Drop your
# own or royalty-free 16-bit PCM WAV here to test locally; audio is never
# committed (licensed/factory samples must not be redistributed). Only the
# folder's README is tracked. See assets/test/README.md.
assets/test/*
!assets/test/README.md

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# Claude Code local overrides
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python bytecode from the tools/ stages (Plan 0106). The stages themselves
# are committed; their caches are not.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Reference render output kept locally (Plan 0106). `shot --render` clips are
# hundreds of megabytes of derived binary; they live here so the evidence behind
# a shipped cost figure outlives the worktree that produced it, and they are
# never committed. renders/README.md says what each one is.
renders/

# Lane spike scratch (Plan 0106). Throwaway spike work lives under spike/ in a
# plan's worktree - renders, venvs, frame dumps, measurement logs. It was
# untracked AND unignored until this close, which is how a test came to read
# spike/clip.wav and pass on exactly one machine (Plan 0106 Phase 7a).
spike/

# The diffusion filter's Python environment (Plan 0106). `docs/diffusion-filter.md`
# tells a creator to build it at the repo root with `python -m venv .venv`, so it
# lands here by instruction rather than by accident - and it is gigabytes of
# platform-specific torch wheels that must never be committed. The tool itself
# (tools/sd-filter/) and its requirements.txt ARE tracked; the environment they
# build is not.
.venv/
